Dr. Beth Garner, played by Jeanne Tripplehorn.

8
00:37:55,555 --> 00:38:01,555
Lieutenant Walker, played by Denis Arndt.

9
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Roxy, played by Leilani Sarelle.

10
00:47:24,444 --> 00:47:30,444
Basic Instinct is a 1992 erotic thriller film directed by
Paul Verhoeven and written by Joe Eszterhas.

11
00:52:08,888 --> 00:52:14,888
It follows San Francisco detective Nick Curran (Michael Douglas) as he investigates the murder of a rock star,
only to begin an intense relationship with the prime suspect Catherine Tramell (Sharon Stone).

12
00:56:53,333 --> 00:56:59,333
The script was developed by Eszterhas in the 1980s and became the subject of a bidding war,
which Carolco Pictures won before bringing Verhoeven on board to direct.

13
01:01:37,777 --> 01:01:43,777
Stone was cast as Tramell after the role was rejected by several other actresses, and production
was plagued by protests and intense conflict between Eszterhas and Verhoeven.

14
01:06:22,222 --> 01:06:28,222
Basic Instinct premiered in Los Angeles on March 18, 1992, and was theatrically
released in the United States by TriStar Pictures two days later.

15
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
It received mixed reviews; praise was given to the performances, score, and
editing, while the script and character development were criticized.

16
01:15:51,111 --> 01:15:57,111
The film also generated controversy due to its depiction of sexually
explicit content, violence, and homosexual relationships.

17
01:20:35,555 --> 01:20:41,555
Despite public protest, it was a commercial success, grossing $353 million worldwide on a
$49 million budget and becoming the fourth highest grossing film of 1992.

18
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
Due to its success and controversy, it inspired many imitators and has been
labelled as "perhaps the quintessential erotic thriller of the 1990s".

19
01:30:04,444 --> 01:30:10,444
Since its release, Basic Instinct has undergone a critical reevaluation.

20
01:34:48,888 --> 01:34:54,888
The film has been recognized for its groundbreaking depictions of sexuality in mainstream Hollywood cinema, and was described by
one scholar as "a neo-film noir masterpiece that plays with, and transgresses, the narrative rules of film noir".

21
01:39:33,333 --> 01:39:39,333
Numerous versions have been released on home video, including a
director's cut with extended footage previously unseen.

22
01:44:17,777 --> 01:44:23,777
Verhoeven considers The Fourth Man as a spiritual prequel to Basic Instinct.

23
01:49:02,222 --> 01:49:08,222
The film was also followed by the sequel Basic Instinct 2 (2006), which starred
Stone but was made without the involvement of Verhoeven or Douglas.

24
01:53:46,666 --> 01:53:52,666
It received negative reviews and was relatively unsuccessful.

25
01:58:31,111 --> 01:58:37,111
The film explores themes of dying and death,
california, jealousy, sexual obsession, police.

26
02:03:15,555 --> 02:03:21,555
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
